character-lifepath-requirement = You must{$inverted ->
    [true]{" "}not
    *[other]{""}
} have one of these lifepaths: {$lifepaths}

lifepath_name_colonial-embryo = Colonial Embryo
lifepath_description_colonial-embryo = The earliest colonial ships entered the jump web before humanity understood drift. They carried no crews—only embryo banks and automation set to grow settlers wherever a viable world appeared.
    Now these vessels surface from the jump web unexpectedly—in empty sectors or above worlds absent on old charts. Automation completes its cycle and releases people with no past or cultural anchor. Their bodies follow old medical standards; their minds are filled with obsolete protocols. Their first days are spent learning current regulations and deciding who to obey just to survive one more cycle in a future that isn’t theirs.

lifepath_name_unemployed = Unemployed
lifepath_description_unemployed = Beneath Alpha’s shining terraces lies the layer the brochures omit: those the system deemed surplus. Washed-out cadets, laid-off workers, anyone whose skills stopped paying off. The walls hear more layoff notices than voices.
    Survival means skirting sensors, swapping access tags, repairing housing from scrap, and keeping income off the books. When inspectors demand evictions, only the neighbor network helps: a warning about raids, a shared meal, patience until the clipboard brigade leaves.

lifepath_name_alpha-coordinator = Alpha Coordinator
lifepath_description_alpha-coordinator = You graduated from an administration academy into a calm but demanding post in an upper sector: personal transport, a clinic, an office with filtered air, and access to briefs. You aligned docking schedules, harmonized orders, and warned services early when data and regulations drifted.
    You greeted inspectors, answered governors and corps, and closed docking windows so no department sat idle. Comfort depended on having paperwork in order before any auditor’s questions landed.

lifepath_name_gs-archive-analyst = GS Archive Analyst
lifepath_description_gs-archive-analyst = You finished data studies and landed in Alpha’s archive center. A clean mid-sector block, onsite clinic, training courses nearby. Your desk stacked daily reports from stations: some stamped by local clocks, others by different beacons.
    You normalized them to GS, checked tables, marked which beacon confirmed the stamp, and explained why local time or jump drift skewed GS. You rang docks and labs to decide which signal to treat as primary and filed justifications when GS needed correction. For most, GS is a line on a form; for you, it’s daily reconciliation and polite-but-firm reminders of its importance.

lifepath_name_barge-recruiter = Barge Recruiter
lifepath_description_barge-recruiter = You lived aboard a recruiting barge: cramped cabin, shared head, a desk beside the medbay and uniform stores. The ship ran a beacon loop—Alpha, Delta, Zeta, Theta, Orpheus—and at every stop you ran the same interviews and checks.
    The corp covered berth, food, and comms, but evenings vanished into reports and nights into listening to docking logs. Your task was staffing a new frontier station. NT paid by headcount: each hire was a contract line, a medical stamp, an NDA signature. You verified clearances and medicals, logged interview results, and drafted contracts on the spot, cutting only those whose access violated NT protocol.
